{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380462-help-with-a-ghoul-focused-game","id":1380462,"title":"Help with a ghoul focused game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-11T13:24:39-07:00","id":1380462,"title":"Help with a ghoul focused game","content":"This is not truly a ghoul chronicle because not all characters are ghouls, some are kinfolk, and hedge sorcerers. But they are a close knit group of allies who try to survive while being low on the totem pole (trust me, the sorcerers are very weak, they are on par with the ghouls).<br /> <br /> <br /> For this session I planned for them to deal with a group of sanguinaries, indepent ghouls who by force or negociations get vitae (they often bribe neonates for the sums of money) and sell it for other independent ghouls.<br /> <br /> The sanguinaries want the players to make a transaction for them. This is the hook I want to use, but I don't know where to go from here, I want the transaction to be the main part of the problem, I want something go wrong and the players having to choose a side, appeasing and helping the sanguinaries, or the vampire.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'v thought about the following scenarios, but I don't know which to use, or how to actually use it for the desired effect.<br /> <br /> - The vampire has a sickness in his blood, so the sanguinaries get pissed. Players are given ultimatum, get good quality nlood or they will be hunted by the sanguinaries.<br /> <br /> - The vampire poisoned the blood, he is actually a camarilla agent who is trying to undermine independet ghouls operations, the sanguinaries think the players are agents of the camarilla.<br /> <br /> -The vampire is not actually a vampire... but a anansi, this one possibility I like just the mindfuck potential but have no idea on how develop it (lol)<br /> <br /> -The vampire actually wants the blood a something rare in exchange for his own, like changeling blood or something, The players will have to get this blood to make the transaction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, anyone have a suggestion on how to make a good use of this hook?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T19:43:50-07:00","id":1380556,"title":"","content":"A neonate does a mass feeding to convert all the blood to vitae in an attempt to blood bond the entire sanguinary group. If the PCs don't discover the plot, then they will be complicit in the blood binding of the entire group. If they fail to stop it, then the mission statement changes to either how to save the group or at least how to get the neonate in trouble.<br /> <br /> Local Tremere are the ones actually selling the blood through a clueless neonate middleman in an attempt to do some blood research on ghouls. Do you stop the rituals or ask for a cut of the action as it were? Perhaps a favor to be named later or just being in the local chantrys rolodex of &quot;trusted&quot; non-tremere contractors.<br /> <br /> Local Malkavian decides to play a prank on the Sanguinaries, either replacing the purchased vitae with his own madness contaminated blood or perhaps that of a nosferatu and laugh while the mutations begin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T22:39:37-07:00","id":1380585,"title":"","content":"Off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> Do all of the player ghouls have the same domitor? Does the domitor have nearly enough blood intake to feed them all? If the sanguinaries do make an offer that the domitor accepts, is one of the players in danger of being drunk dry so that the domitor can churn out as much vitae as the sanguinaries want? Do any ghouls who are competitive for their master's attention have an opportunity to knock their rival(s)? Does a rebellious ghould player have a golden opportunity to break free while all this goes down?<br /> <br /> Note that some of these involve the players bringing something to the table in terms of their characters' motivations, goals, and plans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T21:35:38-07:00","id":1380859,"title":"","content":"All the ghouls in the group are independent, have to hunt or bargain to get blood, etc. But they can act as if they have masters to avoid suspicion. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}